From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:34:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: draw from scratch-memory buffers on the PS Vita,
 re-specify mipmapped textures, time read-backs and presents

vitaGL copies every client-array draw and scans its indices for the highest vertex. Each batch now copies its vertices and indices once into vitaGL's per-frame scratch memory and binds them as buffers that point at that memory (vglBufferData), so the driver neither copies nor scans (GL_SCRATCH_BUFFERS=0 restores client arrays).
A texture with mip levels is re-specified instead of updated in place: a partial update of a mipmapped texture made vitaGL read the old one back from video memory.
gl_timing reports read-backs and the present separately; the line buffer grows to fit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/host/gpu/gl/gl_platform.h b/host/gpu/gl/gl_platform.h
index 75256db..ae449db 100644
--- a/host/gpu/gl/gl_platform.h
+++ b/host/gpu/gl/gl_platform.h
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ static inline void glBlendColor(GLfloat, GLfloat, GLfloat, GLfloat) {}
 #include <GLES2/gl2ext.h>
 #endif
 
+#include <cstddef>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <string>
 
@@ -61,6 +62,26 @@ void destroy_context();
 void swap_buffers();
 [[nodiscard]] Caps &caps();
 // Turns dithering off where the driver has it (GL_DITHER is on by default in ES 2; vitaGL has no such state).
+// Per-frame GPU-visible memory (vitaGL's scratch pool: valid until the GPU has drawn the frame) and handing it to the
+// bound buffer object as its data, so a draw reads vertices and indices in place: the driver neither copies client
+// arrays nor scans the indices for the vertex range. nullptr / no-op where there is no such pool (desktop GL).
+inline void *scratch_alloc(std::size_t bytes) {
+#if defined(__vita__)
+    return vglAllocFromScratch(bytes);
+#else
+    (void)bytes;
+    return nullptr;
+#endif
+}
+inline void buffer_use_mapped(GLenum target, const void *data) {
+#if defined(__vita__)
+    vglBufferData(target, data);
+#else
+    (void)target;
+    (void)data;
+#endif
+}
+
 inline void disable_dither() {
 #if !defined(__vita__)
     glDisable(GL_DITHER);
diff --git a/host/gpu/gl/gl_renderer.cpp b/host/gpu/gl/gl_renderer.cpp
